FreedomCat is a fork. It exists only because of the people who wrote the
projects it is built on.

Upstream lineage
----------------

SagerNet — the original Android proxy client (2021)
  nekohasekai <contact-sagernet@sekai.icu>
  https://github.com/SagerNet/SagerNet
  Contributors: https://github.com/SagerNet/SagerNet/graphs/contributors

NekoBox for Android — the direct base of this fork
  MatsuriDayo
  https://github.com/MatsuriDayo/NekoBoxForAndroid
  Contributors: https://github.com/MatsuriDayo/NekoBoxForAndroid/graphs/contributors

sing-box — the proxy core
  nekohasekai and the sing-box contributors
  https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box
  Contributors: https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box/graphs/contributors

libneko — Go helpers shared by NekoBox
  MatsuriDayo
  https://github.com/MatsuriDayo/libneko

gomobile (Matsuri fork) — builds the Go core into libcore.aar
  MatsuriDayo
  https://github.com/MatsuriDayo/gomobile

AmneziaWG — the obfuscated WireGuard protocol
  AmneziaVPN project and the amneziawg-go authors
  https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amneziawg-go

yacd-meta — the web dashboard
  MetaCubeX
  https://github.com/MetaCubeX/Yacd-meta

shadowsocks-android — inspiration for the Android service layer
  https://github.com/shadowsocks/shadowsocks-android

Format references
-----------------

INCY — public documentation of the subscription, HWID and app-management
headers that device-bound panels expect from clients
  https://github.com/INCY-DEV/incy-docs

FreedomCat
----------

Sergey (sstpnk) — fork maintainer: UI, AmneziaWG support, subscriptions,
build and release plumbing
  https://github.com/sstpnk

Contributors: https://github.com/sstpnk/freedom-cat/graphs/contributors

If you contributed and are missing from this file, open a pull request — the
omission is not intentional.
